{"schemaVersion":1,"kernel":"vector_tour","case":"int8","options":{},"source_path":"kernels/conformance/vector_tour/vector_tour.asm","source":"{#- vector_tour.asm -- native vector tour: 128-element INT8 / FP8 vectors (no\n    emulator-only format).\n\n    A curated conformance program for the Cycle Inspector: it walks the MULT\n    and ACC slots once each on real 8-bit data. It loads a mask, two R_CYCLIC\n    slots and R0/R1, runs MULT.VE, MULT.RC.VV/VS/VE and MULT.EE into\n    ACC.ADD/SUB/MAX, two masked multiplies, and a 4-row matrix-vector loop with\n    AGG.SUM.FIRST. kernel.toml's [abi] says which CR holds what.\n\n    Design notes\n    - The registers are written literally (CR2, not a template binding), so the\n      file is plain assembly: the Inspector shows it as source, and its labels\n      are the source's own.\n    - XMEM from row 0: the four rows of a, then w, c and the R_MASK row (three\n      16-byte slots: all lanes, even lanes, the lower half). acc starts at\n      row 8, as the old harness placed it.\n    - acc is three R_ACC stores of four rows each (one accumulator vector is\n      four rows in an 8-bit format): rows 0-3, 4-7 and 8-11 from CR7. In INT8,\n      relu follows at rows 12-15: ACTIVATE.QUANTIZE RELU through ST.AAQ, whose\n      512 bytes hold the 128 results and then zeros. ACTIVATE.QUANTIZE needs\n      INT8, so CR12 (int8_tail) skips that tail in a float format and the\n      results leave through ST.ACC only.\n    - CR9 is the element scalar 2.0 in the active format; CR11 is ROWS - 1\n      because BLT.S reads the counter from the start of the cycle.\n    - The data (gen.py) is small and exact: INT8 elements are integers\n      in [-8, 8], float elements multiples of 0.25 in [-2, 2], which E3, E4\n      and E5 all hold exactly. Every product and sum is then exact in the\n      INT32 or FP32 accumulator, so every format is compared EXACT.\n-#}\n    SET                 LR0 CR0;\n    SET                 LR3 CR6;\n    SET                 LR1 CR0;;\n    LD.MASK             LR0 CR5;\n    SET                 LR4 CR8;;                                 # LR4 = 4: an R0 element used as a scalar below\n    LD.MULT.CYCLIC      LR0 CR3 LR0;;                             # R_CYCLIC[0..127]   = w\n    LD.MULT.CYCLIC      LR0 CR4 LR3;;                             # R_CYCLIC[128..255] = c\n    LD.MULT             R0 LR0 CR2;;                              # R0 = A row 0\n    LD.MULT             R1 LR0 CR3;;                              # R1 = w\n    MULT.VE             LR0 CR9 0 LR0 CR15;  ACC.ADD.FIRST;;      # R_ACC  = 2 * A0\n    MULT.RC.VV          LR0 R0 0 LR0 CR15;   ACC.ADD;;            # R_ACC += w * A0\n    MULT.RC.VS          LR3 0 LR0 CR15;      ACC.SUB;;            # R_ACC -= c * c\n    MULT.RC.VE          LR3 LR4 0 LR0 CR15;  ACC.MAX;;            # R_ACC  = max(R_ACC, c * A0[4])\n    ST.ACC              LR0 CR7;;                                 # output rows 0-3\n    MULT.RC.VV          LR0 R0 1 LR0 CR15;   ACC.ADD.FIRST;;      # mask slot 1: odd lanes off\n    MULT.EE             LR4 CR9 2 LR0 CR15;  ACC.ADD;;            # broadcast 2 * A0[4]; mask slot 2: upper half off\n    ADD                 LR5 LR0 CR8;;\n    ST.ACC              LR5 CR7;;                                 # output rows 4-7\nmatvec:                                                           # R_ACC[r] = A[r] . w\n    LD.MULT             R0 LR1 CR2;;\n    MULT.RC.VV          LR0 R0 0 LR0 CR15;   AGG.SUM.FIRST LR1 CR15;;\n    ADD                 LR1 LR1 CR1;\n    BLT.S               LR1 CR11 matvec;;                         # LR1 before this word's ADD\n    MULT.RC.VV          LR0 R0 0 LR0 CR15;   AGG.MAX.FIRST LR1 CR15;;   # R_ACC[4] = max(A[3] * w)\n    ADD                 LR5 LR5 CR8;;\n    ST.ACC              LR5 CR7;;                                 # output rows 8-11\n    BEQ                 CR12 CR0 end;;\n    ACTIVATE.QUANTIZE   relu CR15;;                               # INT8 only: clamp(relu(R_ACC))\n    ADD                 LR5 LR5 CR8;;\n    ST.AAQ              LR5 CR7;;                                 # output rows 12-15\nend:\n    HALT;;\n","meta":{"format":"int8","is_float":false,"element_bits":8,"exp_bits":0,"man_bits":0,"accumulator":"int32","emulator_only":false,"lut":null},"trace":{"schema_version":"1.0.0","isa_digest":"7e0d11b257cdf1873b81998a87e480eed040716e2e6ebadf4c54a74d12dcb968","program_digest":"24d12b90d63403d779b78dc8131f22545a204260c4e6ac99fc792e9ac76b9a74"},"program":[{"label":null,"word":"3000000000000318000086000c000018000008040200000","slots":[{"slot":"lr","instance":0,"op":"SET","args":["LR0","CR0"]},{"slot":"lr","instance":1,"op":"SET","args":["LR3","CR6"]},{"slot":"lr","instance":2,"op":"SET","args":["LR1","CR0"]}]},{"label":null,"word":"3000000042040000400004a00c000018000008040200000","slots":[{"slot":"lr","instance":0,"op":"SET","args":["LR4","CR8"]},{"slot":"load","instance":0,"op":"LD.MASK","args":["LR0","CR5"]}]},{"label":null,"word":"3000004000040000400002600c000018000008040200000","slots":[{"slot":"load","instance":0,"op":"LD.MULT.CYCLIC","args":["LR0","CR3","LR0"]}]},{"label":null,"word":"3000004000040000400002806c000018000008040200000","slots":[{"slot":"load","instance":0,"op":"LD.MULT.CYCLIC","args":["LR0","CR4","LR3"]}]},{"label":null,"word":"3000004000040000400000400c000018000008040200000","slots":[{"slot":"load","instance":0,"op":"LD.MULT","args":["R0","LR0","CR2"]}]},{"label":null,"word":"3000004000040000400000602c000018000008040200000","slots":[{"slot":"load","instance":0,"op":"LD.MULT","args":["R1","LR0","CR3"]}]},{"label":null,"word":"300000400004000040000600113e0004000008040200000","slots":[{"slot":"mult","instance":0,"op":"MULT.VE","args":["LR0","CR9","0","LR0","CR15"]},{"slot":"acc","instance":0,"op":"ACC.ADD.FIRST","args":[]}]},{"label":null,"word":"300000400004000040000600001e0000000008040200000","slots":[{"slot":"mult","instance":0,"op":"MULT.RC.VV","args":["LR0","R0","0","LR0","CR15"]},{"slot":"acc","instance":0,"op":"ACC.ADD","args":[